  "resume": "A glass-plate silver bromide negative from the Swiss Army's wartime photographic collection shows a convalescing soldier painting at a garden pavilion in Sigriswil during the First World War. The image documents the soldier's recovery activities rather than combat. It is part of a systematic photographic record of the Swiss Army's activities during the 1914-1918 period."
 },
